  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be two&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;non-zero real matrices such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a zero matrix. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lQ8c4",
      "text": "The system of linear equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;has a unique solution",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4LeFM",
      "text": "The system of linear equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;has infinitely many solutions",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zCoNy",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is an invertible matrix",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mdeZj",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>adj</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is an invertible matrix",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/16510b7f-8907-47de-a9c5-a72f93c83932-image.png\" style=\"width: 158px; height: 90px;\" /></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(not possible)</p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp; (not possible)</p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are non-invertible matrix,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn>&nbsp;has infinitely many solutions</p></blockquote>",
